COLOURMAT-BYTEOFF: car/scene colour tables indexed with byte offsets (pointer-scaling)

FUN_0042b720 (per-car colour/effect update, crash frame after the MulMatrix fixes) writes
`*(undefined2 *)(&car_colour_matrix + iVar2)` with iVar2 = car*0x1e -- a BYTE stride (30 bytes/car;
sibling fields use the raw form `iVar2 + 0x77d206`, byte-correct). car_colour_matrix@0x77d200,
scene_colour_vectors@0x465922, DAT_00465924/26 are int*-typed GIMG macros, so `&SYM + N` scales the
already-byte offset x4 -> writes/reads land 4x too far (observed L8/L10 wild-write SIGSEGV
0xc0796a20/0xbf396a20 in the render loop; scene vectors read the wrong level's row). Byte-address
all arithmetic uses. Same Ghidra pointer-scaling class as CARSTATE/TRACKINFO/CAROBJ-BYTEOFF.

